title A whole build sat in a stash, and the round-open was the one thing reading it
prompt The baton's ordinary open. The card's queue item 1 is REDS %642, and my own claim bakery-scrub-phase-measurement stood live and stale at six hours.
think The round-open's own report named the work: parked in stash@{9} stood active-designing/20260916-121517_where-a-seed-publish-spends-its-minutes.md and tools/fixtures/s/sow_phase_control.sh. That is a complete build -- scan, witness, control, essay, roster row -- from a lap at 12:15 whose send was lost.
think Before reaching for it I asked the absence scan whether a peer had landed it: four paths read here=no upstream=no, absent_both, so the work stood nowhere. Restoring beat rebuilding by every measure, and it beat starting new work by more.
think git checkout stash@{9} -- <path> reads the TREE rather than the blob, so modes arrived intact: both fixture scripts came back 100755 and the witness 100644, which is the exec-bit law's own distinction between a script the tree tells you to run and one invoked through its interpreter.
think Running the restored build on metal rather than trusting it: scan 1.06s, control 27 legs 0 failures, witness GREEN. Nothing had rotted in six hours, which is what a build with no dependency on the day should do.
think Then re-reading the churn at all five spans found something the 12:15 lap could not have seen, because the fleet had been busy then and quiet since. The 1h and 6h spans both answered churn_changed=0 cache_hit_pct=100 -- and both had resolved churn_ref to HEAD itself. A span holding no commit can only read zero.
think That zero and a busy span's zero are two different facts wearing one number, which is the braid this tree already has a word for. So churn_quiet=yes|no|unread joined the reading, planted as a PAIR in the pen because either leg alone passes under a scan that always answers the same word.
obs The control moved 27 legs to 33 and the mutation bites: removing the ref=head comparison fails leg 26 alone, which is the right blast radius for a reading that adds a fact rather than changing one.
obs The elder lap wrote a shelf file for the bakery account the card carried at 12:15 -- and the card had since shelved that account itself and grown a newer one. A shelf written against a six-hour-stale card describes a card nobody has. It was dropped rather than landed, and the account went onto the live card instead.
obs The card had 1,728 bytes of room and the first draft of the account wanted 1,850. Trimming my own newest account rather than folding a peer's is the cheap honest move, and it took three passes to get under.
obs Three session logs stand in the dead-letter box and on no ref, all three this tree's own dead laps. Landing the 20260916 one was in scope; the 20260915 and 20260914 ones want their days' shelves reopened, and a shelf is immutable once its day closes. That is a real question and it is named rather than taken.
rota lap 5112, row 2 -- Fire, the row that sees; looked at what was actually in front of me rather than at the queue, and the round-open's own report was naming a finished build nobody had picked up.
loom witness=sow_phase legs=33 mutations_bitten=5 wall_s=3 scan_s=1.06
loom churn=allow_paths candidates=9050 h12=115 d1=1788 d7=2505 quiet_spans=2
file tools/fixtures/s/sow_phase_scan.sh restored from the stash, plus the churn_quiet reading that tells a quiet span from a still one
file tools/fixtures/s/sow_phase_control.sh restored, and six legs added for the quiet and busy zeros
file tools/s/sow_phase_witness.rish restored, its leg tally moved 27 to 33 so a leg written today is heard today
file active-designing/20260916-121517_where-a-seed-publish-spends-its-minutes.md the measurement, with the quiet zero named and its free figures re-read on arrival
file construction/standing-equipment.kyri the sow_phase row at tier lap
file construction/ITINERARY.md the bakery account, replacing the elder one that had already shelved itself
file session-logs/date/20260916/20260916-121935_measuring-before-caching.kyri the 12:15 lap's own record, landed unedited as the testimony of a lap whose send was lost
scope one parked build recovered, re-proven, sharpened by one reading, and landed; one dead lap's log landed as testimony; no peer file touched
status GREEN -- sow_phase 33 legs on metal and the witness green, exec_bit, ascii_document, unshared_citation, link, link_text_promise and prose_register all green, the roster's sow_phase red closed by re-running the guard, the page A/92
recommend keep-going -- the cache itself is the next lap in this lane: the reading is taken, the key is cheap at 1.24s from the index, and the arithmetic is written down
